config BR2_PACKAGE_TAQ102_DIAG
	bool "taq102-diag (display and LVDS link diagnostics)"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBDRM
	help
	  The three tools that found the panel's shimmer, kept in the image so
	  the next one does not have to be rebuilt and copied in by hand.

	  testpattern paints one dumb buffer and holds it: single-pixel lines,
	  a checkerboard, flat fields. No GPU and no page flips, so anything
	  that moves on screen is the display path rather than an application.

	  lvdsdiag does a clean modeset and then applies one named PHY variant
	  over /dev/mem, which is how the vendor's PLL dividers were compared
	  against ours. phytune walks the PHY's sampling phase with the current
	  setting shown as large blocks, legible even when the link is failing.
